-- title:
--   Scalar commutant of the away-from-r units in M₂(K₀)
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ and $\bar r$ be primes with $\bar r \neq r$, let $N$ be a natural number, and let $a_1, b_1 \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that the quaternion algebra $H = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt` for $\bar r$, that is $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible precisely when $\bar r$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda_1, R_1$ be $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules of $H$ with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order (a subring spanning $H$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and finitely generated, maximal among such), $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection $\Lambda' \cap \Lambda''$ of two maximal orders whose relative index in $\Lambda'$ as additive groups is $N$), and $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$, let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\iota_0 : H \to M_2(K_0)$ an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra homomorphism. Then every $g \in M_2(K_0)$ commuting with $\iota_0(x)$ for all units $x \in H^\times$ belonging to `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v` — the subgroup of those units whose image in $(H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w)^\times$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$, for every height-one prime $w \neq v$ — is of the form $c \cdot 1$ for some $c \in K_0$.
--
--   This is the statement that the commutant in $M_2(K_0)$ of the image of the $\{r,\infty\}$-arithmetic unit group of an Eichler order in a definite quaternion algebra split at $r$ consists of scalars. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph, where it supplies the uniqueness up to scalars of a matrix conjugating one embedding into the other.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_exists_eq_smul_one_of_forall_mem_awayUnits_commute.lean

